// Automatic security updates keep coming from Ubuntu's archive. Ubuntu's
// 50unattended-upgrades allows "${distro_id}:${distro_codename}-security",
// and on Patrone ${distro_id} is "Patrone" (os-release's ID), which none of
// the archive's origins ("Ubuntu") match, so it allowed nothing. These add
// Ubuntu's own, as Ubuntu's file names them for Ubuntu.
//
// And Patrone's own repository (sources.list.d/patrone.sources), installed
// by itself the same way: it's where Ubuntu's security fixes to the packages
// Patrone builds with its changes (GDM, GNOME Settings, first-login setup)
// arrive, since patrone.pref keeps Ubuntu's versions of those out.
Unattended-Upgrade::Allowed-Origins {
        "Ubuntu:${distro_codename}";
        "Ubuntu:${distro_codename}-security";
        "UbuntuESMApps:${distro_codename}-apps-security";
        "UbuntuESM:${distro_codename}-infra-security";
        "Patrone:${distro_codename}";
};
